<title>UK: RUGBY UNION-AUSTRALIA BEAT WALES 28-19.</title>
<headline>RUGBY UNION-AUSTRALIA BEAT WALES 28-19.</headline>
<dateline>CARDIFF 1996-12-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia beat Wales 28-19 (halftime 18-6) in a rugby union international at Cardiff Arms Park on Sunday:</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Australia - Tries: Matthew Burke, Michael Brial, penalty try. Conversions: Burke (2). Penalties: Burke (3).</p>
<p>Wales - Tries: Gareth Thomas. Conversion: Jonathan Davies. Penalties: Davies (4).</p>
</text>
